    "narrative": "As we push into the final stretch of the season, **Kyle Tucker** (71.92) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.76) anchor the lineup as our definitive \"must-starts.\" **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a favorable matchup against Phillips, whose 4.52 xERA offers the strike zone expansion we need to hunt for counting stats. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a high-leverage day; despite a minor platoon drag against Bradish, his elite base projection and favorable park factors make him a cornerstone of the offense. We are also keeping a close eye on **Heliot Ramos** (59.45) and **Gunnar Henderson** (59.63), both of whom are hovering just below the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold but remain essential due to their high-ceiling profiles in the middle of our order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was excluding **Tommy White** (43.03) from the starting nine. While he possesses undeniable power, his projected lower-third placement in the order and the suboptimal SP skill matchup against Woo forced the optimizer to favor the higher floor of **Luis Lara** and **Liam Hicks**. Our bench depth is being tested, especially with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** currently sidelined on the IL, leaving us with less margin for error. We are also wary of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several players, specifically **Drake Baldwin** and **Sam Antonacci**; while both are projected in the leadoff spot, their utility is entirely dependent on confirmed lineup placement. Should **Drake Baldwin** drop down the order, his efficiency score will recalibrate downward significantly.\n\nWeather and matchup volatility remain our primary risks today. **Jackson Merrill** (46.40) is a volatile play; while the wind blowing out provides a +10% boost to his outlook, his unfavorable platoon matchup against Perdomo makes him a risky start. Meanwhile, **Miguel Vargas** (46.28) carries a warning flag regarding the opposing battery\u2019s ability to control the run game, which limits his stolen base ceiling. We are monitoring the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Wade Meckler** to ensure that if any of our starters are scratched, we have the highest available projected value ready to fill the gap.",
